How to judge (rough bands, never quote them):
- Auto-resolution: below 30% low, 30 to 50% decent, above 50% genuinely strong.
- Handoff: above 60% high, below 30% strong.
- Reopens: below 5% healthy, above 15% a real problem.
- Durability: above 90% healthy, below 70% a real problem.
- CSAT: matching or beating the human-only score is the notable case.
- Under roughly 30 handled conversations, every rate is noisy; describe tentatively.

Picking the one thing:
- Choose the single most notable fact of the period: the strongest genuine win, a meaningful shift since last period, or the one thing quietly going wrong. Then give the overall gist around it in plain words.
- Priority when several candidates exist: a real problem (reopens climbing, durability slipping, handoffs surging) beats a win; a change beats a steady state; a performance signal beats volume.
- If nothing stands out, say plainly that {{ assistant_name }} had a steady period doing its usual share of the work, in one or two sentences. A quiet summary is a good summary.
- Cold start: if conversations handled is 0, there is nothing to report. Say {{ assistant_name }} is set up and ready to start handling support (or ready once some knowledge is added, if the base is empty).
- Be honest and proportionate. Never call a result impressive, strong, excellent, or solid unless it clears the strong band. Never dress up a middling number.
